 <a id="provider-owned-semantic-drafts"></a>
 ## Provider-owned semantic drafts
 
+With generation-scoped Sessions, semantic drafts follow `binding.projection` without replacing the input shell. Invalidation cancels old preparation, hydration, checkpoint, and recovery work while preserving the current in-memory document, ordered originals, and unresolved attempt. The lifecycle supplies `projectionGeneration`; tab/source/native ownership and the provider storage key stay stable. A `projection` write checkpoints the preserved record without renewing retention. Providers honor cancellation before every publication. After a ready baseline, editable originals obtain fresh receipts through revision-CAS hydration. Unresolved attempts remain quarantined; nothing sends automatically.
+
 `draftPersistence: 'provider'` opts into `conversation.input.registerDraftProvider(ctx, provider)`. The default is `'stock'`: existing SessionId storage and submission behavior remain unchanged. Provider mode bypasses every shared Conversation localStorage read and write, including view preferences. Registration is exclusive and effect-owned; the provider owns durable storage and authorization, while Conversation owns the editor and transient upload handles.
 
 `DraftScope` names the tab owner, persistent Host context, source, native Session, projection generation and storage key with distinct opaque branded types. Public constructors validate nonempty identities without imposing a native format. A storage key isolates tab/source/native Session and survives refresh or Host restart; a process or projection generation belongs only in the live scope. Decode durable records with `parseSemanticDraftRecord`; unknown fields and receipt-bearing originals are rejected. Ordered logical original references remain separate from runtime readiness, receipts and URLs.
